In the test, `unicode_entities` are created in this order, then converted with `MessageEntity.adjust_message_entities_to_utf_16`. Because the text contains `🙂` before later entities, offsets after that point increase by 1 UTF-16 code unit, so the later bold entity for `"kappa"` becomes offset `54` with length `5`. In `_parse_markdown`, `sorted_entities = sorted(entities.items(), key=lambda item: item[0].offset)`, so the top-level loop visits entities by ascending offset: custom emoji, bold(`beta...theta`), underline, italic, text link, code, spoiler, bold(`kappa`), url, pre. Therefore, at the start of the 8th iteration, `entity` is the second bold entity for `"kappa"`.

## Answer
{"nth_iteration":8,"value":{"length":5,"offset":54,"type":"MessageEntityType.BOLD|||BOLD|||<MessageEntityType.BOLD>"},"variable":"entity"}
